  "note": "Verso page, two-column at the top then single measure. Fig. 1.18 (block n=2) is wide enough to reach x 0.504 - well inside the normal verso measure - so paragraph n=1 is squeezed into a narrow RIGHT column x 0.524-0.904 beside it; left column is x 0.124-0.504. Block n=3 begins in that right column and then wraps to the full measure x 0.313-0.904 once Fig. 1.18 ends, so it is marked `full` and its bbox spans both columns. Blocks n=5..n=10 all use the full measure even though Fig. 1.19 (block n=4, a cyan-tinted area element and a cyan blob surface) stands alongside them: Fig. 1.19 is narrow (x 0.124-0.309) and stays inside the outer margin, so it does not break the measure - the same situation as p006 and p018. Neither figure caption has an A2 block, so both carry n: null; both are cyan #00adef. A footer_rule is present: the short dark #221f1f footnote separator at y 0.8802-0.8815 spanning x 0.313-0.509, above footnote n=10 at about 0.85x body. Block n=8 is Eq. (1.11) with its right-ranged number, hence the bbox to x 0.901. No tinted panel on this page; furniture is the standard verso set with the grey #d1d2d4 running-header panel at top left and the pale cyan folio box at bottom left."
